# ---- AGENTCRAFT local reports (privacy: never commit a user's scan output) ----
# Rationale: an AGENTCRAFT report is the most intimate artifact a user produces.
# These globs keep real scans out of git by default. They intentionally do NOT
# swallow the hand-authored, committed SYNTHETIC fixtures under examples/
# (see negations below).
*.agentcraft.json
*.agentcraft.md
agentcraft-report*.json
agentcraft-report*.md
agentcraft-card*.png
agentcraft-card*.svg
agentcraft-card*.html
# Two-page split: the PRIVATE depth dashboard (page 2) and the redacted shareable
# card (page 1) are scan outputs, never committed. The `*-depth.*` glob catches an
# arbitrarily-named depth twin (e.g. me-depth.png) so a user's private HUD dashboard
# can never be tracked. Page 1 (`*-share.*`) is redacted but is still THEIR scan.
*-depth.png
*-depth.svg
*-depth.html
*-share.png
*-share.svg
*-share.html
/cards/
/out/
/reports/

# ---- PRIVATE build/audit/design docs (local only — never published) ----
# These are the author's internal working notes (methodology, iteration scores,
# raw process). They stay on disk (total-preservation) but are NOT part of the
# public product. The public repo ships only the product surface.
*_REPORT.md
*_AUDIT*.md
*AUDIT_AND_UPGRADE*.md
AGENTCRAFT_V2_*.md
LOOP_*.md
*_LAUNCH_*.md
LAUNCH_*.md

# ---- examples/ is WHITELIST-ONLY (private-by-default) ----
# Anything derived from a real Claude Code history (not a synthetic fixture) is a
# private local scan, never a docs asset. Rather than blacklist private names, we
# ignore EVERYTHING under examples/ (files and subdirs) and then un-ignore ONLY the
# curated synthetic fixtures below. Any new file dropped in examples/ is private.
examples/**
!examples/README.md
!examples/sample-report.agentcraft.json
!examples/sample-report-v2.agentcraft.json
!examples/breach-fixture.json
!examples/agentcraft-card-v2-sample.html
!examples/hero-card.png
!examples/hero-card.html

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- personal test scratch (kept locally, not shipped) ----
_*.py
*-signals*.json
*.bak

# ---- redaction pattern lists (local tools for the pre-push leak check) ----
# Hold the forbidden-token / private-filename regexes so they never live in a
# TRACKED file (otherwise the pattern strings themselves would trip the check).
.redaction-patterns
.private-name-patterns

# ---- operator runbook (Bartek's private publish steps — stays local) ----
# PUBLISH_COMMANDS.md is the author's own push/launch runbook (references a local
# launch doc + personal workflow). It is not part of the shipped product.
PUBLISH_COMMANDS.md
